camchrome: a persona GPU does not refuse failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat.

Over SwiftShader (a host without a GPU, 1000) Chrome refuses a WebGL context requested with
failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat, which exposes software rendering under a renderer string that names
silicon (Clearcote audit: "the GPU named by the renderer string can actually render"). Under a
persona the request to the GPU process drops the flag; getContextAttributes() still returns what
the page asked for. --disable-gpu-fingerprint keeps Chrome's behaviour.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/webgl_rendering_context_base.cc
@@ -209,6 +209,21 @@
 
 namespace blink {
 
+namespace {
+// camchrome (1004): a persona GPU is a hardware GPU. failIfMajorPerformanceCaveat asks for no
+// context when rendering would be software; over SwiftShader (1000) that refusal would expose the
+// software backend the persona's renderer string names as silicon. The page still reads back the
+// attribute it asked for (getContextAttributes); only the request to the GPU process drops it.
+// --disable-gpu-fingerprint (webgl_real) keeps Chrome's behaviour.
+bool PersonaFailIfMajorPerformanceCaveat(bool requested) {
+  if (requested && ungoogled::PersonaActive() &&
+      !ungoogled::CurrentPersona().webgl_real) {
+    return false;
+  }
+  return requested;
+}
+}  // namespace
+
 bool WebGLRenderingContextBase::webgl_context_limits_initialized_ = false;
 unsigned WebGLRenderingContextBase::max_active_webgl_contexts_ = 0;
 unsigned WebGLRenderingContextBase::max_active_webgl_contexts_on_worker_ = 0;
@@ -890,7 +905,9 @@
